# Copy to apps/mobile/.env.local and fill in from your Supabase project
# (Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API Keys). .env.local is gitignored.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_* is the only prefix Expo inlines into the app bundle, so these
# reach the device. Use the PUBLISHABLE key (sb_publishable_...), which is the
# value Supabase now shows where the docs used to say "anon key". The SECRET
# key must never appear in a mobile build - it bypasses Row Level Security.
#
# Mobile is cloud-only: with these unset the app renders a configuration notice
# instead of the product. There is no native local/demo storage fallback.
#
# Metro caches inlined env values. After editing this file, restart with:
#   npm run start --workspace @itera/mobile -- --clear
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
